 "section_summary": "This section contains pages 13 through 80 of a comprehensive statistical roster of educational institutions in Gumma Prefecture, Japan, compiled in the post-World War II period. The tables cover prefectural, municipal, town and village, and private schools across all educational categories, including elementary schools, middle schools, girls' high schools, youth schools, vocational and agricultural schools, kindergartens, colleges, and special schools for the blind and deaf-mute. For each institution, the records specify the official name in Japanese and English, address, founding date, and comparative counts of enrolled students and teaching staff as of April 30, 1946, and November 30, 1946.",
